  "summary": "Four documents directly apply boosted decision-tree ensembles to road traffic flow prediction, satisfying both the method and topic criteria. [V0231] (Gupta et al., 2023) evaluates on the AgriSat-4 dataset, reporting 0.85 accuracy. [V0230] (Fischer et al., 2022) applies the same method to the Atlas-ICU dataset, achieving a test F1 of 0.78. [V0232] (Haddad et al., 2024) reports results on the LedgerGuard dataset with MAE=0.92. [V0229] (El-Sayed et al., 2021) uses the MetroFlow dataset and reports AUROC of 0.71. A fifth candidate, [V0136] (Duarte et al., 2020), applies boosted decision-tree ensembles but to electricity consumption prediction rather than traffic forecasting; it is included as the closest remaining match given the method alignment, though it does not satisfy the topic criterion. Documents such as [V0225], [V0226], and [V0222] address traffic flow but use different methods (decentralised training, self-attention), and are therefore excluded. Documents mentioning boosted decision-tree ensembles for traffic flow only as prior work (e.g., [V0092], [V0010]) are not counted as direct applications.",
